hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"331","Ali bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Abi Al-Madha informed us, saying: Ishaq bin Issa told us, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Asim bin Damrah, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “pray four times before noon.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"332","Abu Al-Ash’ath told us, on the authority of Yazid, he said: Khalid told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, he said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “He would pray four rak’ahs before noon, then he would go out and pray, then he would come back and pray two rak’ahs, then he would go out to sunset, then He returns and prays two rak'ahs.\""
"333","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, that he was asked about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Which of you can stand the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? They said: We would like to know it. He said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “when the sun had set, meaning from its rising, as long as a spear or Two spears, like the amount of the afternoon prayer from its sunset. He prayed two rak’ahs, then gave it a pause, until when the forenoon rose, he prayed four rak’ahs, then gave it a pause. Even when the sun went down, he prayed four rak'ahs before noon when the sun went down, then when he prayed noon, he prayed two rak'ahs after that, and before the afternoon prayer. Four rak'ahs, that is sixteen rak'ahs.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"334","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Asim bin Damrah, he said: I asked Ali bin Abi Talib about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the day after the obligatory prayer. He said: And who can bear that? Then he told him, saying: He used to pray two rak'ahs when the sun rose, and four rak'ahs before noon, making the salutation in the last rak'ah. Four rak'ahs before noon, he makes the salutation in the last rak'ah, and four rak'ahs after it, he makes the salutation in the last rak'ah.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"335","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is bin Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Which of you can bear that? I said: If we do not pronounce it, we hear it. He said: “If the sun is from here, as it was at the afternoon prayer, he prayed two rak’ahs. As it is from here, at noon he prayed four, and he prayed four before noon and two after it, and he prayed four before afternoon, He separates every two rak’ahs with a salutation to the angels brought near, the prophets, and those who follow them of the believers and Muslims.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"336","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Abu Nu’aym told us, he said: Zuhair told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: You will not be able to bear it. We said: So tell us, for we would like to know it. He said: “If the sun was from the east, as is the case with the Asr prayer, he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, then he would give him some time until the sun was from the east.” To its east, like the first prayer, he prayed four rak'ahs, then he went to his family and moved around if he wanted to, then he got up when the sun set. He prays four rak’ahs, then he prays two rak’ahs after noon, and four rak’ahs before the afternoon.”"
"337","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would pray two rak’ahs after every prescribed prayer, except for the afternoon and morning prayers.”"
"338","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “He prayed four rak’ahs during the noon prayer in Medina, and two rak’ahs in the afternoon prayer in Dhu’l-Hulayfah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"339","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jafar told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Utaiba, he said: I heard Aba Juhayfa, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out with the Hijra to Batha’. He performed ablution, prayed the noon prayer two rak’ahs, and the afternoon prayer. “Two rak’ahs, and in front of him was a goat.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Juhayfah ibn Wahb. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"340","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “pray before He prayed two rak'ahs at noon, two rak'ahs after that, two rak'ahs after sunset in his house, and two rak'ahs after evening prayer, and he had not prayed yet. Friday until he finishes and prays two rak’ahs.”"
"341","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, that he heard Asim bin Damra, saying: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he described it and said: “He used to pray four rak’ahs before noon, and after it two rak’ahs. And four rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer, separating each two rak’ahs with salutations to the angels brought near, the prophets, and those Muslims who follow them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"342","Muhammad bin Qudamah told us, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He does not pray a prayer after which he prays unless he prays two rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"343","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim Ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “when he prayed the noon prayer, he would pray two rak’ahs after it, and four rak’ahs before the afternoon prayer.” rak'ahs (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"344","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is bin Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, he said: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he described it, saying: “He used to pray four times before noon and after it.” Two rak'ahs, and he prays four times before the afternoon prayer, separating each two rak'ahs with a salutation upon the angels brought near, the prophets, and those who follow them. The believers and the Muslims.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Ishaq’s name is: Amr bin Abdullah. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: He disagreed with them. Husayn bin Abdul Rahman (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"345","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Husayn bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, On the authority of Asim bin Damrah, he said: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he described it, saying: He used to pray before noon. Four rak'ahs, he makes the tasleem in the last rak'ah, and after that four rak'ahs, he makes the tasleem in the last rak'ah.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"346","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Kathir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad bin Al-Haad, on the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer in my house, so I said: What are these two? He said: “I used to pray them before the afternoon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"347","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Anba Mansour, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Muslim, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri said: “We were contemplating the rise of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon and afternoon, so we conjectured that he would stand at noon for thirty days.” Verse, the value of Surat Al-Sajdah in the first two rak’ahs and in the last two rak’ahs was half of that, and we estimated his standing in the first two rak’ahs of The afternoon prayer is at the same time as the other two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer, and we estimated his standing in the other two rak’ahs of the afternoon prayer at half of that.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Awana disagreed with him."
"348","Suwayd bin Nasr bin Suwayd told us, he said: Abdullah told us, on the authority of Abu Awanah, on the authority of Mansour bin Zazan, on the authority of Al-Walid, Abu Bishr, on the authority of Abu al-Mutawakkil, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to get up at noon and recite thirty Qur’anic prayers. A verse in each rak’ah, and he stands in the afternoon prayer for the first two rak’ahs, amounting to fifteen verses.”"
"349","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, and Ibrahim bin Maysarah, they heard Anas bin Malik say: “I prayed four rak’ahs with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, at noon in Medina and two rak’ahs in the afternoon at Dhu al-Hulayfa,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Ibn Al-Munkadir's name is: Muhammad, and he has three sons, Omar bin Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, Al-Munkadir bin Muhammad bin Al-Munkadir, and Yusuf bin Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir, Omar Ibn Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir is trustworthy, and Al-Munkadir Ibn Muhammad Ibn Al-Munkadir is not strong, his memory is bad, and Yusuf Ibn Muhammad is nothing in the hadith (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"350","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Mas’ar, Ibn Abi Khalid, and Al-Bakhtari bin Abi Al-Bakhtari told us, They all heard it from Abu Bakr bin Amara bin Ruwaybah Al-Thaqafi, on the authority of his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “No one who prays before sunrise or before sunset will enter Hell.”"
"351","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram told us, he said: Hibban bin Hilal told us, he said: Habib told us, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd. On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went outside, then he was married and did not wake up until the sun rose, or part of it, and he did not He prayed until the sun rose, so he prayed, which is the middle prayer.”"
"352","Ubaid Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: Al-Zabarqan bin Amr bin Umayyah told me, A group of Quraysh were sitting, and Zayd ibn Thabit passed by them. They sent two of their servants who asked him, and he said: It is noon. He said: Then they turned to Usama bin Zayd asked him, and he said: It is the noon prayer. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the noon prayer in the Hijrah and the people in I will lead them and lead them, and there will be nothing behind it except a row and two rows. So God sent down “Guardians of the prayers and the middle prayer.”"
"353","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Hakim told me, he said: I heard Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the noon prayer. He migrated, and he did not pray a prayer more severe for the Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, than it. So, “Guard the Prayers and the Middle Prayer” was revealed. And he said: “There are two prayers before it, and two prayers after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"354","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Anba Isa bin Yunus, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Muslim bin Subaih, on the authority of Shutair bin Shikal, on the authority of Ali, He said: They occupied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, from the afternoon prayer until he prayed it between the two evening prayers. He said: “They distracted us from the middle prayer, may God fill Their houses and their graves will be a fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"355","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Hassan On the authority of Ubaida, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"356","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Yahya bin Adam, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Zirr, he said: We said to Ubaidah: Ask Ali asked about the Wusta prayer, so he asked him, and he said: We used to watch it at dawn, and I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying on the Day of the Ahzab: “They have distracted us from... The middle prayer, the afternoon prayer, “God will fill their graves and their bodies with fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"357","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abu Dawud told me, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, on the authority of Zahra, he said: We were Sitting with Zayd ibn Thabit, he was asked about the middle prayer, and he said: “It is the noon prayer.” Then Usama ibn Zayd passed by us, so we asked him, and he said: “ It is the noon prayer, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray it in the afternoon prayer.”"
"358","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Othman bin Othman Al-Ghatfani told me, and he was trustworthy, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: I was among a people who disagreed about the middle prayer, and I was the youngest of the people. He said: So they sent me to Zayd bin Thabit to ask him about the middle prayer, so I came to him and asked him, and he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray the noon prayer in the Hijra. And the people were in their villages and markets, and no one would pray behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, except one row and two rows, so God revealed: Preserve the prayers and the middle prayer and stand up to God in obedience. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Some people will cease, or I will burn their houses.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is an error, but the correct one is: Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of al-Zabarqan ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabet, and Osama bin Zaid (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"359","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abu Al-Nadr told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, said: “The middle prayer is the noon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"360","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “The one who He misses the afternoon prayer as if he were taking care of his family and wealth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"361","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Abu Qalabah, he said Abu Al-Malih told me, and he said: We were with Buraidah on a cloudy day, and he said, “Get up early to pray, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said “Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his work has been vain.”"
"362","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “What you miss The afternoon prayer is as if he had provided for his family and wealth.”"
"363","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, on the authority of Abu Yunus, the client of Aisha, He said: Aisha ordered me to write a Qur’an for her, and she said: When you reach this verse, inform me: “Guard the prayers and the middle prayer.” When I reached her, I gave her permission and she turned to me. “Reserve the prayers, the middle prayer, and the afternoon prayer, and stand up to God in obedience.” She said: I heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"364","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God did not leave May God bless him and grant him peace, I have never performed the two rak’ahs after the afternoon prayer in my house.”"
"365","Ahmad bin Mani’ told us, he said: Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Qatada, he said: Abu Al-Aliyah, and his name is Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: I heard more than one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, among them, Omar, and he was one of the most beloved to me. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “forbade prayer after dawn until the sun rises, and prayer after afternoon until the sun sets.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Tawus disagreed with him, and he narrated it, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and he did not mention Omar. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"366","Ahmad bin Harb told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Hujayr, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He said, “He forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"367","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Anbasa told us, he said: Wahib told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, He said: Aisha said: Omar is delusional, but “the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade one to check the rising or setting of the sun.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"368","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Saeed bin Amir told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Nasr bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of his grandfather Muadh, he was with Muadh bin Afra and he did not pray, so I said: Don’t you pray? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “There is no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets, and no prayer after the dawn prayer until the sun rises.”"
"369","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Wahb ibn al-Aja``, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade prayer after the afternoon prayer unless the sun was white and high."
"370","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Ali, who is Ibn Mushar, informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, On the authority of Aisha, she said: “There are two prayers that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not leave in my house, secretly or in public: two rak’ahs before dawn and two rak’ahs \"After the afternoon\""
"371","Ali bin Uthman bin Muhammad bin Saeed bin Abdullah bin Nufayl told us, he said: Saeed bin Issa told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us Bin Al-Qasim, he said: Bakr bin Mudar told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, that Abu Al-Khair, told him, that Abu Tamim Al-Jishani “stood up to perform two rak’ahs before sunset, so I said to Uqba bin Amir: Look at this man, what prayer is he praying?” So he turned around. He went to him and saw him, and he said: “This is a prayer that we used to pray at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"372","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Khams, who is Ibn al-Hasan, he said: Abdullah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Mughaffal said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Between every two calls to prayer is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer is a prayer, between every two calls to prayer is a prayer.”"
"373","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I prayed with the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him in Medina, eight in all, and seven in all. He delayed the noon and hastened the afternoon, and delayed the sunset and hastened the evening. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"374","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Salamah, he said: I saw Saeed bin Jubayr in a crowd. He stood and prayed three rak'ahs of sunset, then he stood and prayed two rak'ahs, then he mentioned that Ibn Umar did that, in that place, and he mentioned that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did something like that in that place.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"375","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn, who is bin Ali, told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, Nafi’ said, Abdullah said: “I prayed He performed two prostrations with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, before noon, two prostrations after it, two prostrations after sunset, and after the evening prayer. “Two prostrations, as for Maghrib, Isha’, and Friday prayers, then on his journey.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"376","Al-Hussein bin Abdul Rahman informed us, he said: Abba Talaq bin Ghannam said: Abba Yaqub, who is the son of Abdullah Al-Qummi, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to prolong the two rak’ahs after sunset.”"
"377","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Zayd bin Hubab told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Maysara, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, On the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I prayed Maghrib with him and he prayed until the evening prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"378","Al-Hussein bin Mansour bin Jaafar told us, he said: Hussein bin Muhammad told us, he said: Israel told us, and Ahmad bin Suleiman told us He said: Zayd ibn Hubab narrated to us, and the pronunciation is his. He said: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Maysara, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Zirr ibn Hubaysh, on the authority of Hudhayfah, said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I prayed Maghrib with him and he prayed until the evening prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"379","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him “He prayed seven and eight prayers in Medina, noon, afternoon, sunset, and evening, combining the two prayers.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"380","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’atha’, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “I prayed behind the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, eight in all and seven in all.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"381","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam informed me, he said: Sa`id bin Jubayr led us in prayer. “By joining the Maghrib prayer three times, with the Iqamah, then the salutation, then he prayed the evening prayer with two rak’ahs.” Then he mentioned that Abdullah bin Omar did that, and he mentioned The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did that."
"382","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz bin Asad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, he said: Salamah told us, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, he said : I saw Abdullah bin Omar praying in congregation, then he stood and prayed the Maghrib prayer three times, then he prayed the evening prayer with two rak’ahs. Then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God. May God bless him and grant him peace. He made"
"383","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Al-Hasan told us, he is the son of Musa, he said: Shayban told us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim. On the authority of Yahnas, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If only people knew what is in the dark prayer, And the morning prayer will come to them even if they crawl.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"384","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muslim bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Aban bin Yazid told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told us On the authority of Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If only he would teach the people what is in these two prayers,” Then he mentioned a word that means “I would have brought them to their senses even if they had crawled.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"385","Nuh bin Habib told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, one night, Omar called him and said: The women and children were asleep, so he went out to them and said: “What is this woman waiting for?” “Prayer was performed by none of the people of the earth other than you,” and prayer was not performed on that day except in Medina. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"386","Nasr bin Ali bin Nasr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Ala, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, spent dinner, until Omar called him: The women and children had slept, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out. He greeted him and said: “No one prays this prayer except you.” And at that time no one was praying except the people of Medina."
"387","Nusayr ibn al-Faraj told us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn al-Sabbah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of al-Mughirah ibn Salman, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: I memorized ten prayers from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, two rak’ahs before dawn, and two rak’ahs before dawn. “Dhuhr, two rak’ahs after noon, two rak’ahs after sunset, and two rak’ahs after dinner.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"388","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled bin Al-Harith told us, on the authority of Malik, who is Ibn Mughal, on the authority of a fighter, who is Ibn Bashir, On the authority of Shuraih bin Hani, he said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “There was no prayer more worthy of He delays it if he is following a hadith of the evening prayer, and he never prayed it and entered upon me except that he prayed four or six after it.”"
"389","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labid, trustworthy, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha, on the authority of the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “She wanted to pray at night. His prayer during the month of Ramadan and at other times was thirteen rak’ahs.” From it are the two dawn rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"390","Al-Harith bin Miskin told us, as I read it while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Al-Qasim, he said: Malik told me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salama bin Abdul-Rahman, that he told him that he asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, what was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace in Ramadan? She said: He did not pray more than eleven rak'ahs, during Ramadan or at any other time, and he prayed four, so do not ask about their beauty or length. Then He prays four, and you are not asked about their beauty or length. Then he prays three. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God, do you sleep before you pray Witr? He said: “O Aisha, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Abu Sa`id, his name is: Kaysan."
"391","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Saeed bin Abi Saeed Al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Salamah bin Abdul Rahman, that He told him that he asked Aisha, the Mother of the Believers, how was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during Ramadan? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak’ahs in Ramadan or at any other time. He would pray four, so do not ask about Their beauty and length, then he prays four, so do not ask about their beauty and length, then he prays three. Aisha said: So I said: O Messenger of God Do you sleep before you feel stressed? He said: “My eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.”"
"392","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Othman told us, he is Ibn Omar, he said: Anba Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night, eight rak’ahs, and perform Witr with three rak’ahs. And he performs the two rak’ahs of Fajr.”"
"393","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, that Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah, Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani told him that he said: “To enhance the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He prayed two light rak’ahs, then prayed He performed two long, long, long rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were inferior to the ones before them, then he prayed two rak'ahs, which were inferior to those before them. He kissed them, then he prayed two rak’ahs, which were less than those before them. Then he prayed two rak’ahs, which were less than those before them.”"
"394","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night at my aunt Maymunah’s, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, got up during the night and fulfilled his need, then washed his face and hands. Then he fell asleep, then he got up and went to the waterskin and loosened its noose, then he performed ablution between the two ablutions. He did not do much, but he had completed it. Then he He stood up and prayed, so I stood up and performed ablution, so he stood up to pray, so I stood to his left, so he took my ear and turned me to his right, and the Messenger of God’s prayer was completed. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he prayed thirteen rak’ahs, then he lay down and slept until he blew, and when he slept, he blew and Bilal came to him and called him to prayer, so he stood up. So he prayed but did not perform ablution, and he used to say in his supplication: “Oh God, put light in my heart, and light in my hearing, and light in my sight, and light on my right hand, and To my left is light, above me is light, below me is light, in front of me is light, behind me is light, and give me the greatest light.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"395","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, that Ibn Abbas told him He spent the night at the house of Maimuna, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she was his maternal aunt. He said: So I lay on the width of the pillow and he lay The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his family during its entirety, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slept until, at midnight, or A little before it or a little after it, then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up, and he began wiping the sleep from his face with his hand, then He recited the final ten verses of Surah Al Imran, then he got up to a hanging hangar, performed ablution from it, and performed his ablution well, then he stood up to pray. Ibn Abbas said: So I got up and did the same as he did, then I went and sat next to him, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed his hand My right ear was on my head, so he took my right ear and twisted it, so he prayed two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then two rak'ahs, then He prayed two rak'ahs, then prayed the Witr prayer, then he lay down until the muezzin came to him, so he stood up and prayed two short rak'ahs, then he went out and prayed the Fajr prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"396","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth narrated to us, he said: Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abu Hilal, on the authority of Makhramah bin Sulaiman, that Kurayb, the client of Ibn Abbas, told him, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas, I said: How was the prayer? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night? He said: “He used to recite on his lap, and whoever was behind him could hear his recitation,” and he said: “He spent the night with him while he was with Maimuna bint Al-Harith. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Maimunah lay on a pillow made of human hair, stuffed with fiber. They lay on its length, and I lay on the length of it. He exposed it and they slept, until when a third or half of the night had passed, he woke up, and he got up and went to a container with water in it, and he performed ablution, and I performed ablution with him, then He got up and I stood next to him on his left, so he put me on his right and put his hand on my head. He started wiping my ears as if he were waking me up, so he prayed two rak’ahs. Two light ones. I said: He recited in them the Umm al-Qur’an in every rak’ah, then he said the salaam, then he prayed two rak’ahs, then he said the salaam, until he prayed eleven. He performed a rak'ah with the witr, then he fell asleep until he became heavy and I saw him blowing the strings. Then Bilal came to him and said: Prayer, O Messenger of God, so he stood up and prayed two rak'ahs and prayed. for people and did not perform ablution.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"397","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Anba Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night in the house of Maimuna, “Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood up and prayed during the night, so I stood up with him on his left, and lo and behold, by my hand, he made me stand on his left side.” \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"398","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abu Jamrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “He used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"399","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yahya bin Adam told us, he said: Abu Bakr al-Nahshali told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to pray eight rak’ahs at night, and perform the Witr prayer with three rak’ahs.” He prays two rak’ahs before the Fajr prayer.”"
"400","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ali Ibn Abdullah Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “So he got up and performed ablution and fasted, and he He recites this verse until he finishes it. Indeed, in the creation of the heavens and the earth and the alternation of night and day are signs for those of understanding, until he recited these verses, or he reached the end of the surah, then he prayed two rak’ahs, then he went back to sleep until I heard him blowing it, then he got up and performed ablution and sat still, then he prayed He prayed two rak'ahs, then he fell asleep, then he got up, performed ablution, sat down, prayed two rak'ahs, and performed Witr with three.” Abba Muhammad ibn Jablah said: Muammar ibn Makhlid narrated to us and he was trustworthy. He said: Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up, and he straightened his feet and recited the hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"401","Qutayba bin Saeed told us, Othman bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would pray two rak’ahs, then he would leave and fast.” Othham said: He meant the two rak’ahs. Before dawn"
"402","Muhammad bin Ali bin Maimun told us, he said: Al-Qanabi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz, who is the son of Muhammad Al-Darawardi, told us, on the authority of Abdul Al Majeed, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, that Ibn Abbas narrated to him, that his father Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib sent him The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was in need of him, and Maimuna bint Al-Harith was the maternal aunt of Ibn Abbas, so he entered upon her and found the Messenger of God God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, in the mosque. Ibn Abbas said: So I lay down in its room, and I kept to myself to count how many times the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace? He said: Then he came while I was lying in the room after the night had passed, and he said: The newborn lay down and he took a quilt on Maymunah’s bed. He said: So he dressed He performed some of them and one on top of them, then he stood up and prayed two rak’ahs, until he prayed eight rak’ahs, then he performed Witr with five, without sitting between them, then he sat So he praised God for what He deserved, then he praised more, and at the end of his words he said: “O God, put a light in my heart for me and make Light in my hearing and place for me light in my sight, and place for me a light on my right and a light on my left and place for me a light before me and a light behind me and increase me with light.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"403","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Al-Hakam told me, he said: I heard Saeed bin Jubayr, He narrates, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abbas, who said: “I spent the night at my aunt Maimuna’s house,” so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the evening prayer, then came So he prayed four times, then he slept, then he got up and performed ablution. He said: I do not remember his ablution. Then he got up and prayed, so I stood to his left, so he placed me on his right. Then he prayed five rak’ahs, then two rak’ahs, then he slept, then he prayed two rak’ahs, then he went out to pray.”"
"404","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I spent the night in the house of my aunt Maimuna bint Al-Harith, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and said: “The boy fell asleep after he prayed.” He prayed four evening prayers after that, then he prayed the night prayer and I came and stood on his left, so he pulled me and placed me on his right, so he prayed five times. rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs, then he slept until I heard his snoring, or his whispering, then he went out to pray.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"405","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam told us, he said: Muhammad bin Ja’far told us, he said: Musa bin Uqba told me, On the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amer al-Sha’bi, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas and Ibn Omar, how was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night? They said: “Thirteen rak’ahs, and perform the Witr prayer with three rak’ahs, and two rak’ahs after dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"406","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Al-Shu’abi, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he “would pray thirteen rak’ahs at night.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"407","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told us, he said: Othman told us, he is Ibn Omar, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Umm Salamah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night, eight rak’ahs, and perform Witr with three rak’ahs, and bow The two rak'ahs of dawn\""
"408","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdul Rahman told us, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha, How many prayers did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray? She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray more than eleven rak’ahs in Ramadan or at any other time, and he did not pray four.” Ask about their beauty and length, then pray four, but do not ask about their beauty and length, then pray three.”"
"409","Hisham bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is Ibn Hamzah. He said: Al-Awza’i told me, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: Aisha told me that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would pray eight rak’ahs after Isha’, then pray Witr, then pray “Two rak’ahs in which he recites while sitting, so if he wants to kneel, he gets up and kneels, then after that he performs the two rak’ahs of Fajr.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"410","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of bin Abi Labid, he heard Abu Salamah say: I asked Aisha about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “He used to fast in Sha`ban except for a short time.” I asked her about his prayers at night, and she said: “His prayers were at night during the month of Ramadan. And in others there are thirteen rak’ahs, including the two rak’ahs of Fajr.”"
"411","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Yunus told us, meaning Ibn Muhammad, the discipliner, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid, On the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that he heard Aisha say: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would pray every three nights.” He performed ten rak'ahs, nine while standing, and two rak'ahs while sitting, then he would give time until he called the call to prayer on the first day of the morning. He got up and bowed two rak'ahs.\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"412","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Sa`id, who is the son of Abi Ayyub, told us, he said: Ja`far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Arak ibn Malik, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the evening prayer, then he prayed eight rak'ahs, standing, two rak'ahs sitting, and two rak'ahs between the two calls, and he did not miss them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"413","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib, on the authority of Arak bin Malik, on the authority of Urwa, that Aisha told him that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “pray thirteen rak’ahs with the two rak’ahs of dawn.”"
"414","Qutaibah bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, used to “pray eleven rak’ahs at night, of which he would pray Witr with one of them. When he finished it, he would lie on his right side.”"
"415","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh told us, he said: Abba ibn Wahb, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib, Yunus, and Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, Ibn Shihab told them, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray while he finished his prayers. From the evening prayer until dawn there are eleven rak'ahs. He says the salutation in every two rak'ahs, prays the Witr prayer with one rak'ah, and prostrates as many prostrations as he recites. One of you recites fifty verses before he raises his head. Then, when the muezzin is silent during the Fajr prayer and the dawn becomes clear to him, he gets up and performs two rak’ahs. And he lay on his right side until the muezzin comes to him for the establishment and he comes out with him.” And some of them add to others in the story of the hadith."
"416","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was “He prays thirteen rak’ahs at night, then when he hears the call to dawn he prays two light rak’ahs.”"
"417","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba bin Sulayman told us, he said: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray thirteen rak’ahs at night, performing Witr with five of them, and not sitting in any of the five. Except at the end of them he sits and greets.”"
"418","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Hanzalah, that he heard Al-Qasim speaking, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He prays ten rak’ahs at night, then prays the Witr prayer with one rak’ah, then performs two rak’ahs at dawn.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"419","Muhammad bin Ali bin Harb Al-Maruzi told us, he said: Hisham bin Abdul-Malik told us, he said: Husayn bin Nafi’ told us. Al-Anbari, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray eight rak’ahs, and perform the Witr prayer.” At the ninth hour, when he arrived, he prayed six rak’ahs, performed Witr with the seventh, and prayed two rak’ahs while sitting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"420","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Saad bin Hisham, he said: I presented Medina, so I went to Aisha, and she said to me: Who are you? So I said: I am Saad bin Hisham. She said: May God have mercy on your father. I said: Tell me about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was strengthened. I said: Yes, but tell me. She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was strengthened. And peace be upon him, “He leads the people in prayer for the afterlife, then he goes to bed. When it is the middle of the night, he gets up to purify himself and performs ablution, then He entered the mosque and prayed eight rak'ahs, equating them with recitation, bowing and prostration, then he performed Witr with one rak'ah, then he prayed two rak'ahs while he was He was sitting, then he laid down his head. Perhaps Bilal came to him and called him to prayer before he fell asleep, and perhaps I doubted whether he had fallen asleep or not until he called him to prayer. By prayer, and that was the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, until he became old and flesh-faced, so he used to pray with the people in the dark, then he would go to In his bed, when it was the middle of the night, he got up to purify himself and performed ablution, then he entered the mosque and prayed six rak’ahs, making them equal in bowing. And prostration and recitation, and he prays two rak’ahs while sitting, then he lays on his side, and perhaps he does not doze off until Bilal comes and calls him to prayer, and perhaps I doubted whether he had forgotten or not.”"
"421","Ismail bin Masoud told us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Saeed told us, he said: Qatada told us, on the authority of Zurara bin Awfa, on the authority of Saad Bin Hisham, that Abdullah bin Abbas came and asked him about the Witr prayer, and he said: Shall I not direct you to the most knowledgeable people on earth regarding the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God? May God bless him and grant him peace. I said: Who? He said: Aisha, go to her and ask her, then come back to me and inform me of her response to you. So we went to Aisha and asked her permission. So we entered. I said: O Mother of the Believers, inform me about the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: Do you not read the Qur’an? I said: Yes, she said: “For the character of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the Qur’an,” so I decided to get up and not ask anyone about anything until I die."
"422","I said: Tell me about the resurrection of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: “Do you not recite this surah, O distinguished one?” I said: “Yes.” She said: “For God assumed the beginning of this surah in the Day of Resurrection, so He rose.” The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and his companions spent a year until their feet swelled, and God withheld its end for twelve months in heaven, then God revealed the mitigation at the end of this Surah, so praying the night prayer became voluntary after an obligatory prayer. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"423","I said: O Mother of the Believers, tell me about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: We used to prepare for him his ablution and use of the siwak, and God would raise him up whenever He wished, to raise him up at night so he could cleanse himself and perform ablution, then He prays nine rak'ahs, during which he does not sit until the eighth, in which he praises his Lord and supplicates to Him and remembers Him. Then he gets up, without salaaming, and prays the ninth. So he sits and remembers his Lord and praises Him and supplicates to Him, then he says the salutation in a way that makes us listen, then he prays two rak’ahs while sitting after he has salutated. Those are eleven, my son. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, established the Sunnah and took the meat, he prayed seven rak’ahs, not sitting except in the last of them. He prayed two rak'ahs, while he was sitting after he had said the salutations. Those are nine, my son. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer, he liked to He would perform it regularly, and the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, if he was preoccupied with a matter or overcome by sleep or pain, he would pray twelve days during the day. One rak’ah, and I do not know that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited the entire Qur’an in one night, nor did he stand in prayer for a night until the morning, nor did he ever fast an entire month. Other than Ramadan.” So I went to Ibn Abbas and informed him of her hadith, and he said: She spoke the truth, but if I had entered upon her, I would have come to her until You tell me about it verbally. I said: If I had known that you would not come to her, I would not have informed you of her story. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"424","Ahmad bin Sulaiman told us, he said: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Wathhab, on the authority of Masruq, said: I asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night, and she said: “Seven and nine And eleven rak’ahs, in addition to the two rak’ahs of the morning.”"
"425","Hanad bin Al-Sirri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “He prays nine rak’ahs at night.”"
"426","Ahmad bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Ala’, who is Ibn Usaym, told us, he said: Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amara bin Umair, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, on the authority of Aisha, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray nine rak’ahs at night, but when he increased his flesh and teeth and prayed seven rak’ahs.”"
"427","Hanad bin Al-Sari informed us, on the authority of Abu Muawiyah, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murrah, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Umm Salamah, She said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Witr prayer with thirteen rak’ahs, but when he grew old and weak, he performed the Witr prayer with nine rak’ahs."
"428","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told me, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, On the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray the Witr with nine rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"429","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Hammad told me, he said: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, On the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “used to pray the Witr with nine rak’ahs.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"430","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, meaning bin Zuray’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: I told Maqsim, “I hear the call to prayer, so I pray Witr with three, then I go out to pray for fear that I will miss it. He said: This is not suitable except with seven or five.” So I narrated that to Mujahid and Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, and they said: Ask him about whom? So I asked him, and he said: Trustworthy on the authority of Trustworthy, on the authority of Aisha and Maimunah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"431","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yahya, who is the son of Adam, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, On the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Umm Salamah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “would perform the Witr prayer with five or seven rak’ahs, not separating them with words or salutations.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"432","Amr bin Hisham told us, he said: Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Muqasim, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, On the authority of Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform the Witr prayer with seven and five rak’ahs, not separating them with a greeting or a word.”"
"433","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “used to perform the Witr prayer with five prayers, not sitting except in the last of them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"434","Ali bin Hajar told us, he said: Anba Sharik, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And peace be upon him: He used to say “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers,’ and say, ‘He is God, the One,’” in a rak’ah. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"435","Ahmad bin Suleiman told us, Abu Nu’aym said, he said: Sharik told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He used to recite the string with “Glorify the name of your Lord Most High, and say, ‘O disbelievers, and say, ‘He is God, the One’.”"
"436","Ahmad ibn Abdah told us, he said: Hammad told us, on the authority of Anas ibn Sirin, he said: I said to Ibn Umar: Have you considered the two rak’ahs before the prayer? In the morning, should I read for a long time? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray two by two during the night, and pray the Witr prayer with one rak’ah, and he would pray the two rak’ahs before dawn as if The call to prayer with his ears"
"437","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked He mentioned the night prayer, saying: “Two by two, and if you fear the dawn prayer, then one.”"
"438","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: The night prayer is two by two, so when the dawn approaches, pray Witr with a rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"439","Ishaq bin Musa Al-Ansari told us, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, he said: The Messenger said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Indeed, God is a string and loves the string, so perform the string, O people of the Qur’an.”"
"440","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, he said: “It is not The Witr is definitely like the obligatory verse, but it is a Sunnah that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, enacted.”"
"441","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiya told us, he said: Dabbarah bin Abi Al-Sulaik told me, he said: Dawayd, he is Ibn Nafi’, told me. He said: Ibn Shihab told me, he said: Ata’ bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The Witr “Truly, whoever wishes may pray the witr with seven, and whoever wishes may pray the witr with five, and whoever wishes may pray the witr with three, and whoever wishes may pray the witr with one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"442","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud told us, he said: Abdullah bin Yusuf told us, he said: Al-Haytham bin Humaid told us, he said: Abu Mu’eed, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, said: Ata’ bin Yazid told me that he heard Abu Ayyub say: “The witr is a right, so whoever likes to pray the witr with five rak’ahs, let him do so, and whoever likes to pray the Witr with three rak’ahs, let him do so, and whoever likes to pray the Witr with one, let him do so.” Abu Abdul Rahman: Abu Mu’id, his name is Hafs bin Ghaylan, and he is a good hadith narrator."
"443","Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, he said: Hajjaj bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abdul Rahman He is Ibn al-Qasim. He narrated it, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The night prayer Two by two, then if you want to leave, kneel one rak’ah to make up the length of the prayer for as long as you have prayed.”"
"444","Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Anba Abd al-Rahman, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “he would pray eleven rak’ahs at night, of which he would perform Witr with one of them, then he would lie on his right side.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"445","Yahya bin Musa Al-Balkhi told us, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Khalid told us, he said: Saeed bin Abi Arouba told us, on the authority of Qatada, On the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ubayy ibn Ka`b, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was And peace be upon him, “It is recited in the Witr prayer with “Glorify the Name of your Lord Most High,” and in the second rak’ah with “Say, O disbelievers,” and in the third with “Say He.” God is One, and He does not greet except in the last of them, and He says after the salutation: Glory be to the Holy King three times."
"446","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad told us, he said: Sa`id told us, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Rahman bin Abza, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “praise the name of your Lord, the Most High, and Say, O disbelievers, and say: He is God, the One. Then when he finished his Witr prayer, he said: Glory be to the Holy King.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"447","Zakaria bin Yahya told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Abba Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara Bin Awfa, that Saad bin Hisham bin Amer, when he came to us, told us that he had come to Ibn Abbas and asked him about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God. God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Shall I not guide you or inform you of the most knowledgeable people on earth regarding the ritual uterus of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? I said: Who? He said: Aisha, so we went to her and we greeted and entered. I asked her and said: Tell me about the Witr prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace? She said: We used to prepare for him his siwak and his ablution, and God would raise him up whenever He wished to raise him during the night. He would use his siwak and perform ablution, then he would pray. Nine rak'ahs in which he does not sit except in the eighth, then he praises God and remembers Him and supplicates to Him, then he gets up and does not say the salutation and prays the ninth, then he sits. So he praises God, remembers Him, and supplicates to Him, then he gives the salutation so that he can hear us, then he prays two rak’ahs while sitting, and that is eleven rak’ahs. That is, my son. When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Sunnah and took the meat, he prayed the Witr prayer with seven rak’ahs, then prayed two rak’ahs while sitting after the salutation. Those are nine, meaning my son, and when the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed a prayer, he liked to continue it.”"
"448","Zakaria bin Yahya al-Sijistani told us, he said: Ishaq told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: I am Muammar, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Saad bin Hisham told me, on the authority of Aisha, that he heard her say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to perform the Witr prayer. He prayed nine rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs while sitting. When he became weak, he prayed Witr with seven rak'ahs, then he prayed two rak'ahs while sitting."
"449","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abba Muadh bin Hisham, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, he said: Abu told us Salamah, that he asked Aisha about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: “He used to pray eight rak’ahs, then pray Witr, then pray Two rak’ahs while he was sitting, so he would recite and bow, and pray two rak’ahs between the call and the iqama of the morning prayer.” Ja’far bin Rabi’ah followed him."
"450","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Sagha’i told us, he said: Yunus told us, he is the son of Muhammad, the teacher Al-Baghdadi, he said: Laith told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Ja’far bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that he heard Aisha say: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray every night. Thirteen rak'ahs: nine standing and two rak'ahs while sitting, then he gave a period of time until the call to prayer was called on the first day of the morning. He got up and prayed two rak'ahs,\" he said. Abu Abd al-Rahman: Sa`id entered between Ja`far and Abu Salamah, Arak ibn Malik. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"451","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Sa`id told us, he said: Ja`far bin Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of A’rak bin Malik, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the evening’s prayer, then he prayed eight rak’ahs standing, He bowed two times sitting, and bowed two bows between the two calls, and he did not miss them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"452","Amr bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, he said: Malik told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Abu Salamah, he said: I asked Aisha, about the prayer The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not exceed eleven days in Ramadan or at any other time.” One rak’ah, he prays four, and you will not be asked about their beauty or length, then he prays four, and you will not be asked about their beauty or length, then he prays three.”"
"453","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Labid, with Abu Salamah, saying: I asked Aisha about the fasting of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. She said: “He used to fast in Sha’ban except for a short time.” I asked her about the night prayer, and she said: “His prayer was at night in the month of Ramadan and at other times, there are thirteen rak’ahs, including the two rak’ahs of Fajr.”"
"454","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, he said: Ismail bin Khalil told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida reported, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jesus Bin Abi Azzah, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Abu Thawr al-Azdi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “commanded that the two rak’ahs be performed before Fajr prayer\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"455","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata’ told me, on the authority of Ubaid bin Umair, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not more keen on performing any of the voluntary prayers than he was about performing the two rak’ahs before dawn.”"
"456","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Khaled told us, meaning Ibn Al-Harith, he said: Shu’bah told us, that Ibrahim bin Muhammad He told him, he said: I heard my father speaking, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, “would not leave the four days before noon. Nor the two rak’ahs before the morning prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"457","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sa`id, and Sulaiman al-Taymi, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Zurara, on the authority of Sa`d ibn Hisham, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The two dawn rak’ahs are dearer to me than the whole world.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"458","Qutayba bin Saeed informed us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu Laznad, on the authority of Al-Araj, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, He said: “Angels succeed one another among you at night and angels during the day, and they gather for the dawn prayer and the afternoon prayer, then he ascends.” Those who spent the night among you, then He will ask them, and He knows best about them, How did you leave My servants? They will say: We left them while they were praying, and We came to them while they were praying. They pray\""
"459","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Qais told me, he said: Jarir bin Abdullah told me, He said: We were sitting with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he looked at the moon on the night of the full moon and said: “But you will see your Lord as You see this, if you are able not to neglect a prayer before the sun rises or before it sets, then do so. Then he recited and glorified with praise. your Lord before the rising of the sun and before its setting.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"460","Kathir bin Ubaid told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The congregational prayer is superior to the prayer of one of you alone in twenty-five parts. “The angels of the night and the angels of the day in the dawn prayer, and recite, if you wish, the recitation of the dawn prayer. Indeed, the recitation of the dawn prayer was witnessed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"461","Amr bin Ali and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ismail, he said: Abu Bakr bin Amara bin told me. Ruwaybah, on the authority of his father, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “No one who prays before sunrise and before \"set down\""
"462","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told us, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Ezra bin Tamim, on the authority of my father Hurairah, that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you prays one rak’ah of the morning prayer, then the sun rises, let him pray another rak’ah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"463","Abu Dawud told us, he said: Abu Al-Walid told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Qatada was asked about a man who prayed one rak’ah of the morning prayer. Then the sun rose, and he said, Khalas bin Amr told me, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, that Abu Hurairah told him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: “He will complete his prayer.”"
"464","Abd al-Hamid bin Muhammad told us, he said: Mukhlid bin Yazid al-Harrani told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yazid said that he heard Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “There is no prayer after the last prayer.” Fajr prayer until the sun rises, and no prayer after the afternoon prayer until the sun sets.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"465","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Baqiyyah told us, on the authority of Buhair, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, on the authority of Nu’aym bin Hammar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: God says: “Son of Adam, kneel four rak’ahs at the beginning of your day, and I will suffice you at the end of it,” Abu Abd said. The Most Gracious: He brought alcohol between many and the bliss of Qais al-Jazami."
"466","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi’ told us, he said: Bishr told us, he said: Bard told us, on the authority of Sulayman bin Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Kathir ibn Murrah al-Hadrami, on the authority of Qais al-Judhami, on the authority of Nu’aym ibn Hammar al-Ghatfani, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of His Lord, Almighty and Majestic, said: “The son of Adam, pray four rak’ahs at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice for you at the end of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"467","Harun bin Abdullah told us, he said: Ma’an told us, he said: Muawiyah bin Salih told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Kathir bin Once, on the authority of Nu`aym, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God Almighty said: “Son of Adam, do not fail to perform four rak’ahs of prayer.” At the beginning of the day, I will protect you at the end of it.” He told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman bin Dawud, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yusuf, on the authority of Al-Haytham bin Humaid, on the authority of Abi Al-Ala bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Kathir bin Murrah, with it"
"468","Harun bin Abdullah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ishaq, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Murrah al-Taifi He said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: God Almighty says: “Son of Adam, perform four rak’ahs at the beginning of the day, and I will suffice for you at the end of it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"469","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to “perform the forenoon prayer.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"470","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khalid told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, that he heard Asim bin Damra, he says: We asked Ali about the prayer of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, during the day, and he said: You cannot bear it if the sun is from here. Meaning the East, as it looks from here, meaning the West, at the afternoon prayer he prayed two rak'ahs, and when the sun was from here, meaning The East, as it is from here, meaning the West, at noon, he prayed four, and he used to pray four before noon, and after it Two rak'ahs, and four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer, and each two rak'ahs should be separated by greeting the angels who are close to Him, the prophets, and those who follow them. \"Muslims\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"471","Wasil bin Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Abi Suleiman, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim Ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, said: The Prophet of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, “when the sun had passed its setting, used to tie a spear, or two spears.” As for the duration of the afternoon prayer from its sunset, he prayed two rak'ahs, then he gave it a pause until when the noon prayer had risen, he prayed four rak'ahs, then he gave it a pause until when the time had passed. He prayed four rak'ahs before noon when the sun had set, so when he prayed noon, he prayed two rak'ahs after that, and four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer. That is sixteen rak'ahs. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"472","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, and Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, they said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, that he heard Ali al-Azdi, that he heard Ibn Umar, narrating, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “The night and day prayers are two Muthanna,” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: This is a good chain of narration, but the companions of Ibn Umar disagreed with Ali al-Azdi. Salim and Nafi’ disagreed with him. And a peacock (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"473","Amr bin Uthman told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “The night prayer is two by two, so when the dawn approaches, pray Witr with one.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"474","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Khalid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The night prayer is two rak’ahs, and the Witr prayer is a rak’ah.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: Khalid ibn Ziyad ibn Jaz’ Khurasani, trustworthy and upright in hadith."
"475","Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, he said: Al-Mu`tamir informed us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked He mentioned the night prayer, saying: “Two by two, so if you fear the dawn prayer, then one.”"
"476","Bishr bin Hilal Al-Sawwaf Al-Basri told us, he said: Abdul-Warith told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Tayyah, on the authority of Abu Uthman Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah He said: My friend Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace, advised me to do three things: fasting for three days of every month, and performing Witr before sleep. And the two rak'ahs of the forenoon"
"477","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan told us, he said: Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Asim bin Kulayb, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: “I have never seen the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the Duha prayer.”"
"478","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Shu’bah told me, on the authority of Fudayl bin Fadalah, he said: Abd told me Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father, that he saw people praying the forenoon prayer, and he said: “This is the prayer that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not pray.” And neither did most of his companions."
"479","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Khaled told us, he said: Saeed told us, on the authority of Qatada, that Muadhah told them, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to pray four times the forenoon prayer or more as God willed."
"480","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I did not see the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, always prays the morning prayer, and I praise it, even though the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to give up work even though he loved to do it. “For fear that people will do it and it will be imposed on them.”"
"481","Ahmad bin Musa Al-Marwazi told us, he said: Abba Abdullah is Ibn Al-Mubarak, he said: Abba Khaled Al-Hadha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq He said: I asked Aisha, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pray the noon prayer? She said: “No, unless he comes from his absence.”"
"482","Ubayd Allah bin Fadhalah bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Yusuf bin Al-Majishun told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Asim. Ibn Omar Ibn Qatada, on the authority of his grandmother Rumaitha, who said: I was with Aisha in the morning, and when we woke up, she got up and took a bath, then she entered a house. So she closed the door and said: O Mother of the Believers, I have not spent the morning with you except for this hour. She said: So enter. She said: So I entered. So she stood up and prayed eight rak’ahs. I do not know whether they were standing longer or if they were kneeling or prostrating. Then she turned to me and hit my thigh and said: “O Rumaythah, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying it, and if my parents were told to abandon it, I would not have abandoned it.” And on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah On the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Yaqoub ibn al-Ashjaj, on the authority of al-Qaqaa ibn Hakim, that Rumaitha bint Hakim told him that she had come to Aisha. . . . . He mentioned it as suspended (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"483","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, he said: I asked to find someone He told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swam during his journey, but I did not find anyone to tell me that, until Umm Hani bint told me Abu Talib said, “The year of the conquest came and he ordered that it be covered, then he prayed eight rak’ahs of tasbih.”"
"484","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Abdullah told us, he said: Al-Rabi’ bin Rawh told us, he said: Muhammad bin Harb told us, on the authority of Al-Zubaidi, on the authority of Al-Zuhri said: Abdullah bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal told me that his father said: Umm Hani is the daughter of Abi Talib She told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was staying there on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he came one day after the day had risen.” So he ordered a bath, and it was poured for him, then he was covered, so he bathed, so he got up and said the takbir, then he prayed eight rak’ahs. I do not know whether he stayed in them longer or longer. Is his bowing, and is his bowing in them longer, or is his prostration all of them close together, and I have not seen him do that before or after.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"485","Muhammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ibn Wahb told us, he said: Yunus bin Yazid told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah told me Bin Abdullah bin Al-Harith, that his father Abdullah bin Al-Harith bin Nawfal told him, that Umm Hani bint Abi Talib told him, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came after daylight had risen on the day of the conquest, “and he ordered a garment to be put on and he was covered with it, and he bathed, then he got up.” He kneeled eight rak'ahs, and I do not know whether he stood longer, or bowed, or prostrated. All of that was close together. She said: I did not see him praising her. \"Before or after\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"486","He informed us on the authority of Muhammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, on the authority of Amr bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Bukayr bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Dahhak bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi narrated to him, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, who said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey. He prayed eight rak’ahs of the morning prayer, so when He left and said: “I prayed a prayer of desire and awe, so I asked my Lord for three things, and He gave me two and withheld from me one. I asked him not to kill me.” “I led my nation for years, and he did so. I asked him not to make their enemy prevail against them, and he did. I asked him not to confuse them with sects, but he refused.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"487","Amr bin Yazid told us, he said: Bahz told us, he said: Shu`bah told us, Amr said, meaning Ibn Murrah, he told me, he said: I heard Ibn Abi Laila said: No one reported that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, praying the noon prayer except Umm Hani, for she mentioned the day Conquest of Mecca, he “bathed in her house, then prayed eight rak’ahs. She said: I did not see him praying a lighter prayer than her, except that he was performing bowing and prostration”"
"488","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Yazid told us, and he is Ibn Zurai’, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Nu’man bin Salim, on the authority of Amr bin Aws, on the authority of Anbasa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habibah, who said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever prays twelve rak’ahs every day voluntarily, not obligatory, a house will be built for him in Paradise.” On the authority of Humayd ibn Masada, on the authority of Bishr Ibn Al-Mufaddal, on the authority of Dawud Ibn Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Nu’man Ibn Salim, on the authority of Muhammad Ibn Rafi’, he said: Zayd Ibn Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Saeed Al-Taifi told me, he said: Ata bin Abi Rabah told us, on the authority of Ya’la bin Umayyah, he said: I came to Al-Taif and entered Anbasa. Ibn Abi Sufyan, as he was dying, and I saw his distress, so I said: You are doing well. He said: My sister, Umm Habibah, told me that the Messenger God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever prays twelve voluntary rak’ahs during the day or at night, a house will be built for him in Paradise.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"489","Humayd bin Masada told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he is Ibn Habib, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, On the authority of Omar, he said: “The Friday prayer is two rak’ahs, the breaking of the fast is two rak’ahs, the sacrifice is two rak’ahs, and the journey is two rak’ahs, complete without shortening it according to the words of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” May God bless him and grant him peace. “Yazid bin Ziyad bin Abi Al-Ja’d entered between Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila and Omar Ka’b bin Ajrah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"490","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Yazid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Zubaid al-Yami, on the authority of Abdul Rahman Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b Ibn Ujrah, said: Omar said: “The Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak’ahs. The traveler’s prayer is two rak’ahs, complete and not shortened, according to the words of your Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he who fabricates inventions will be disappointed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"491","Ibrahim bin Muhammad told us, he said: Yahya told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, he said: He said Omar: “The traveler’s prayer is two rak’ahs, the Eid al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Fitr prayer is two rak’ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak’ahs. It is complete and not short on the tongue.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"492","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj told us, he said: Ibn Idris told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Adi, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “went out on the day of Eid and prayed two rak’ahs. He did not pray before or after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"493","Muhammad bin Bashar told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Adi bin Thabit, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “went out and prayed on the day of Adha. He did not pray before or after it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"494","Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, he said: Al-Layth bin Saad told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: Salik Al-Ghatfani and the Messenger of God came God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was sitting on the pulpit, and Salik sat down before praying, and the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to him: “You prayed two rak’ahs.” He said: No. He said: Get up and kneel on them. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"495","Imran bin Musa told us, he said: Yazid bin Zurayi told us, he said: Sufyan bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Zubaid al-Yami, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, that he mentioned it, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, who said: “Al-Adha prayer is two rak’ahs, the Breakfast prayer is two rak’ahs, and the traveler’s prayer Two rak'ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs.\" It is complete and not short on the tongue of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
